      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. Their problem was that saved searches returned low-relevance hits and duplicates, increasing manual triage time significantly. To get them comfortable with renewal, we proposed a short-term mitigation proof plan involving updating index weighting and adding a translation/mapping layer for the top 20 saved searches. This plan includes a 7-10 business day A/B test and validation aiming for a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, followed by a 1-day production rollout and a 72-hour monitoring window. Additionally, a professional services engagement was offered at a fixed price of $48k with a 30% discount if Orchestrator expansion is signed concurrently. There is also a conditional credit on renewal if the proof does not meet acceptance criteria within 10 business days [art_bd3560dfe194, art_0bccc580184e].",
