      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments,\" causing ingestion normalization to fail collapsing these into a single canonical attribute, which led to the Rules Engine failing to match the entity tag for routing approvals. Jin proposed a fast fix by adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded without requiring Okta change control, avoiding delays of 2\u20134 weeks for Okta source standardization. This approach allows immediate remediation with low risk and no appliance restarts during settlement windows by targeting non-peak nodes for collector process restarts only. [art_79f625aafa16]",
